# What git may do to a tracked file on the way in and on the way out.
#
# Settled now, while the tree is small, because it stops being a small file the
# day the data directories fill up. A change of line-ending policy after a few
# hundred data files exist is a diff touching every one of them, which nobody
# can read and which hides any real correction that lands beside it.
#
# The policy is one sentence: everything is text, stored with line feeds, and
# checked out with line feeds on every platform. `eol=lf` is what makes the
# second half true regardless of the clone's `core.autocrlf`, and it is there
# for Windows specifically. Without it a contributor with conversion enabled
# sees every tracked text file reported as modified on a tree they have not
# touched, which makes a real formatting defect indistinguishable from noise.
#
# On exact bytes. Normalisation is applied to everything here on purpose, and
# that is a problem for one kind of test: a fixture that exists to prove a
# parser refuses a malformed byte sequence is exactly the thing normalisation
# silently repairs on the way into git. The rule is that such a fixture is
# encoded in source, as bytes the compiler produces, rather than stored as a
# file, and the reason is written next to it. Declaring `-text` for a fixture
# directory would be the other way to do it and is deliberately not taken: it
# moves the exactness into this file, where the test cannot see it, and a later
# edit here would silently change what the test proves.
#
# A new extension gets a line below. The catch-all is the floor rather than the
# answer, so an extension nobody declared is still normalised, and
# `git check-attr text eol -- <path>` never answers `unspecified`.

* text=auto eol=lf

# Source and manifests.
*.rs    text eol=lf
*.toml  text eol=lf
*.lock  text eol=lf

# Prose and configuration.
*.md    text eol=lf
*.yml   text eol=lf
*.yaml  text eol=lf
*.json  text eol=lf

# Files whose whole name is the extension.
.gitignore     text eol=lf
.gitattributes text eol=lf
.editorconfig  text eol=lf
